! mcp_bootstrap_p224.strap -- MCP printed page 224: the Input Program's
! request section (V REQ6 .. V CEOJ), lines 1-50.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.231, read at 400 dpi, 900 dpi for
! doubtful glyphs.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID CA000472  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 224"; the heading
! row's LOCATION field is 224516, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  50 lines, every one located, contiguous from 224516.00 to
! 224547.00 (a half word; next 224547.40), then blank paper.  Every
! LINE number prints with a "*" after it; lines 1, 23 and 46 also print
! a "*" after the LOCATION.  Remarks run -0478 .. -0520 (octal-free
! decimal here), except line 15, which prints "-011" where -0490 would
! fall; no row prints -0510 (lines 38, 39 print none).  Line 50 prints
! "-OVERLAPPED" before its -0520.
!
! >>> "REQ", NOT "REG". <<<  At 400 dpi the labels V REQ6/9/10/11 and the
! references V REQ5/V REQ7 look like G; at 900 dpi every one has the
! diagonal tail of the Q in V Q2 / V Q4 (lines 8, 11, 18, 20), which
! the binary pins as index registers $5 / $13 (.13/.12, .72 = X1 .40 +
! 2*13).  Same for V RQ11A (line 24 label, line 15 reference) and V EQ.
!
! LINE 4 "VF,C" IS VF,0.  Printed 000000.00+; the open round is the
! drum's worn 0 (line 3's SIC,0 and line 38's V+I,V T5,0 print the
! same glyph closed).  The labels V BEOJ / V SEOJ / V CEOJ are written
! with O, as landed p.215 wrote VBEOJ (224533.0, this page's line 26);
! V CEOJ's first glyph has no left stem (unlike the D of V RDQ), so C.
!
! V POP comes from this page's binary only: BZB's bit address prints
! 224107.62 = V VSCR (224105.00) + 2.50, so V POP = 2.32 and ".18"
! adds 18 bits.
!
! Octal-field opens ("CCCCCC.00+", "224516.CC") are 0.  Card serials
! CA000472 .. CA000515 printed with a stemless "0A"-looking prefix
! (recorded as the header's CA).  Shared serials: lines 5/6 (476),
! 9/10 (479), 16/17 (485), 21/22 (489), 27/28 (494), 47/48 (513).

